{"channel": "cookbooks", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-01-14T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "the llm interface refactor landed and it has broken some of the examples, I'm working through which ones are actually affected so we can get ws-016 fixes in today", "id": "m-cookbooks-2025-01-14-197", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "🔧"}]}
{"channel": "releases", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-01-14T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "\"v0.1.15 is out\" just went to the team. I also flagged in it that appending to the input dataset between restarts is a trap, I had 200 rows added to an 800-row set and the resumed job came back with 800 results for 1000 requests, reassembly slotted by index, and half the rows had somebody else's answer without any sign of it on inspection.", "id": "m-releases-2025-01-14-258"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-01-14T09:00:12+00:00", "text": "the main thing I wanted on record: there is exactly one function that decides whether a row is reused or sent, and every processor calls it, online, batch and the local vLLM one, so any change there is a breaking change to every persisted cache and has to be treated that way", "id": "m-code-review-2025-01-14-990"}
{"channel": "releases", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-01-14T09:03:43+00:00", "text": "@emil where are the release notes for 0.1.15 at, and do they cover the caching-and-resume changes?", "id": "m-releases-2025-01-14-259"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "petar", "created_at": "2025-01-14T09:04:12+00:00", "text": "config validation fixes are wrapped up and ready for eyes, want to make sure they go in clean beofre end of day, example updates are all done too so 0.1.15 should be in good shape", "id": "m-code-review-2025-01-14-991", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "✅"}]}
