{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-01-16T12:41:49+00:00", "text": "Opened the release-and-ci postmortem (Jan 10), root cause is still tagged as pending Dermot's WS-014 workstream, so that one isn't closed on my side yet. If Dermot's got what he needs from the CI logs I can fill the gap, otherwise it's waiting on him.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-01-16-591"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-01-16T13:40:49+00:00", "text": "Opened the cache hashing postmortem (Jan 13) too. It's there and the root cause is well documented. Batch is explicitly called out as one of the three processors hitting the same hash function, so yes, the regression touched us. The code comment flagging all three callers went in already.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-01-16-592", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "✅"}]}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-01-16T13:40:54+00:00", "text": "Two action items still open from that doc: the resume test and the cache versioning question", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-01-16-593"}
