{"channel": "code-review", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-02-10T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "PR 481 is up for review, it adds manual cost-map support for providers that don't have standard pricing, so you can pass in your own token costs. Touches provider-integrations. Not blocking a release but I'd like to get it in today.", "id": "m-code-review-2025-02-10-1400"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-02-10T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "- *bulk-llm-inference*: stable, nothing new from my end over the weekend\n- *multimodal-prompts*: making progress but I still need to align on the pickler strategy before I can move forward, not entirely sure what the right fallback approach is\n- want to take a look at PR 481 scope this morning too, need to understand how far the cost-map feature is supposed to reach", "id": "m-engineering-2025-02-10-1132"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-02-10T09:00:12+00:00", "text": "@Emil what was the revert this weekend, I saw 4 commits land but didn't catch what got rolled back", "id": "m-engineering-2025-02-10-1133"}
