{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-02-24T13:50:07+00:00", "text": "Worth a quick sync to nail down the warn vs block question, anyone free this afternoon?", "id": "m-engineering-2025-02-24-1376"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "gideon", "created_at": "2025-02-24T13:50:21+00:00", "text": "I think I lean block honestly, a warn that gets scrolled past and then every row 400s anyway doesn't feel like much of an improvement.", "thread_id": "m-engineering-2025-02-24-1372"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-02-24T13:51:05+00:00", "text": "I'm not sure block is right either though, if someone intentionally tweaks the model mid-run they're going to want some rows to go through, not a hard stop.", "id": "m-engineering-2025-02-24-1378"}
