{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "gideon", "created_at": "2025-03-26T16:06:31+00:00", "text": "that silently returns 0 if usage isn't where it expects it", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1452"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-26T16:06:54+00:00", "text": "I'm not sure shipping with that zero fallback counts as cost tracking actually being in place.", "thread_id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1452"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-26T16:07:07+00:00", "text": "I'm still not comfortable calling it \"in place\" while the main verification gap is just deferred.", "thread_id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1452"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-26T16:28:07+00:00", "text": "Honestly, I'd lean toward marking the VCR test as deferred rather than calling cost tracking done with a silent zero fallback", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1455"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "gideon", "created_at": "2025-03-26T16:55:07+00:00", "text": "so who's actually fixing the extraction before we call it done?", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1456"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-26T17:17:07+00:00", "text": "If usage comes back at the job level instead of per result, distributing it across individual results is a meaningfully different problem than just changing where we look.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1457"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-26T17:37:07+00:00", "text": "We could store job-level usage and divide evenly across results as a stopgap until we have a fixture to test against", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1458"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "gideon", "created_at": "2025-03-26T18:11:07+00:00", "text": "want to sync on this tomorrow morning?", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1459"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "gideon", "created_at": "2025-03-26T18:11:15+00:00", "text": "not going to land the stopgap approach in chat tonight", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-26-1460"}
