{"channel": "engineering", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-31T11:27:24+00:00", "text": "WS-050: Batch Mode (50%-Cost Async Batch APIs) is up on the engineering wiki. The main thing I wanted settled before this milestone closes: went through every batch ticket from the last two months, and every failure died while waiting on the provider, laptop lid, CI runner hitting its six-hour cap, OOM killer, one power cut. Nobody has ever managed to die inside the submit call itself, that thing returns in about 200ms. The risk is entirely in the poll window, and resume has to be built around persisted job IDs because of it. That's the design position, it's in the doc now.", "id": "m-engineering-2025-03-31-1701", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "📋"}]}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T11:31:31+00:00", "text": "Confirmed on my end too, resume and retry are untouched by the auth changes, I went through online-request-processing specifically and the auth path stays provider-side the whole way.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1468"}
