{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T15:11:00+00:00", "text": "Once PR 565 gets a sign-off, that's the last thing I'm waiting on to call the provider side of this milestone done.", "id": "m-engineering-2025-03-31-1711"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T15:42:55+00:00", "text": "Good call on the poll-window framing for the batch resume design, Emil", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1480"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-31T15:54:00+00:00", "text": "If someone has credentials for some providers but not others, they're going to get provider-specific errors at request time rather than a clear upfront failure, a preflight credential check at initialization would catch that earlier.", "id": "m-engineering-2025-03-31-1712"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "theo", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:00:00+00:00", "text": "for Mistral batch the api key gets checked at submission so a missing credential surfaces pretty early at least on that provider", "id": "m-engineering-2025-03-31-1713"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:04:55+00:00", "text": "Fine to close on auth and retry/resume, but issue 207 is still open on this channel and Mistral batch makes it more pressing.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1481"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:05:36+00:00", "text": "On issue 207, the `has_capacity` implementation relies on rate limit headers from provider responses, and Mistral batch returns different headers than the online endpoint", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1482"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:05:41+00:00", "text": "Right now nobody owns a fix and it's not in any open PR", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1483"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:05:46+00:00", "text": "It's not blocking the current milestone since we're not gating on it, but if we're adding more batch providers this is going to keep coming up and it's not something that'll resolve itself.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1484"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:07:46+00:00", "text": "Issue 207 is also unowned and there's no agreed approach for it yet, so that's going to stay stuck until someone picks it up", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1485"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:18:46+00:00", "text": "Dario already said what I was going to say, issue 233 is in the same boat, nobody owns automatic rate limit detection either.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1486"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:36:00+00:00", "text": "Honestly I'm not sure a preflight check at init is the right place for it, credentials can be valid at startup and revoked by the time a request goes out", "id": "m-engineering-2025-03-31-1714"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:39:29+00:00", "text": "Do we want to assign owners to issue 207 and issue 233 now or carry them into the next milestone as unowned?", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1487"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:39:57+00:00", "text": "I'd lean toward carrying both into next milestone rather than assigning owners at the end of the day with no real discussion, but i dunno if others feel differently", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1488"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "theo", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:46:57+00:00", "text": "@Dario Kestrel since you just went through online-request-processing, can you add a note to issue 207 on where the fix would actually need to land before we carry it forward", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1489"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:47:39+00:00", "text": "You mean a comment on the issue itself, not just a note here in chat?", "thread_id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1489"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T16:47:58+00:00", "text": "Once Theo confirms he wants it on the issue, I'll add the note there and then both 207 and 233 can go into next milestone with at least some context attached", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1491"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "konrad", "created_at": "2025-03-31T17:16:00+00:00", "text": "Good. Examples, auth, and Mistral batch all current on my end so I'm done here.", "id": "m-engineering-2025-03-31-1715", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "✅"}]}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "theo", "created_at": "2025-03-31T17:16:58+00:00", "text": "yup on the issue itself, and once that's done I think we're good to close out the day on this one, Mistral batch is production-safe and the pipeline paths are all confirmed unaffected", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1492", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "🎯"}]}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T17:30:58+00:00", "text": "Solid end to the day, auth and Mistral batch are in good shape and the pipeline paths held", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1493", "reactions": [{"author": "dermot", "emoji": "👍"}]}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-03-31T17:31:10+00:00", "text": "I'll put that note on issue 207 first thing tomorrow", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-03-31-1494"}
