{"channel": "engineering", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-04-18T14:51:12+00:00", "text": "Same shape of thing with max_tokens for me - response came back truncated mid-sentence, I raised max_tokens, reran, and got handed the same truncated text again. Ended up deleting the whole cache directory, which took out four thousand rows that were perfectly fine.", "id": "m-engineering-2025-04-18-1952"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-04-18T14:51:24+00:00", "text": "This was local - is the expectation that people bust the whole cache when generation params change, or should changing max_tokens be invalidating on its own?", "id": "m-engineering-2025-04-18-1953"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-04-18T14:51:44+00:00", "text": "To be clear on the sequence: truncated mid-sentence with max_tokens, raised max_tokens, reran, got handed the same truncated text again.", "id": "m-engineering-2025-04-18-1954"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-04-18T14:52:04+00:00", "text": "Deleting the cache directory is what finally cleared it, and that took out four thousand rows that were perfectly fine along with it.", "id": "m-engineering-2025-04-18-1955"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-04-18T14:53:24+00:00", "text": "Yeah", "id": "m-engineering-2025-04-18-1956"}
{"channel": "engineering", "author": "dario", "created_at": "2025-04-18T14:53:36+00:00", "text": "that's current behavior in caching-and-resume - max_tokens isn't part of the cache key", "id": "m-engineering-2025-04-18-1957"}
