{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "PR 693 is up for streaming support on the online requests path, touching bulk-llm-inference. Would appreciate a first pass from anyone familair with how we handle the online concurent request flow.", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2985"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "Been looking at PR 693 against the bulk-llm-inference side and I'm not entirely sure whether streaming runs through a separate code path or shares the same routing logic as the standard online requests", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1849"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T09:00:12+00:00", "text": "Wanted to flag that before we get too far along", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1850"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T09:04:17+00:00", "text": "@Emil, is PR 693 a separate code path for streaming or is it integrated with the existing online request handling?", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2986"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T09:08:23+00:00", "text": "@Emil, after the auto batch mode changes, does streaming go through the same routing decision or is it treated separately?", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1851"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T10:17:17+00:00", "text": "Ok", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2987"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T10:17:29+00:00", "text": "answering my own question - looked at the PR and `fetch_response_streamed` unifies the output to look like a normal response, so it's essentially a separate path within the online processor", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2988", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "✅"}]}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T10:17:41+00:00", "text": "Does it handle a mid-stream drop, or does that just fail outright?", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2989"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T10:23:09+00:00", "text": "Ok", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1852"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T10:23:14+00:00", "text": "partly answering my own question, from the PR it looks like streaming stays within the online processor and the output is unified, so presumably the routing decision happens before that", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1853"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T10:23:19+00:00", "text": "Is the batch vs online split still just based on provider support, or did auto batch mode change that logic?", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1854"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T10:26:41+00:00", "text": "The retry behavior on a mid-stream drop is still an open question for me, not sure if that's addressed somewhere in PR 693 or if it's left for a follow-up.", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2990"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T11:20:19+00:00", "text": "Still waiting on that one", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1855"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T11:22:58+00:00", "text": "That one's still open, presumably a follow-up commit", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2991"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-06-26T12:00:19+00:00", "text": "My read is that streaming forces online anyway, so the auto batch decision tree doesn't really apply to it at all", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1856", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "✅"}]}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-06-26T12:00:24+00:00", "text": "Does your question extend to cache behavior too, or is it strictly about the routing split?", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1857"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-06-26T12:05:32+00:00", "text": "When you say \"separate path within the online processor\", is `fetch_response_streamed` a parallel implementation, or does it share the upstream routing and only diverge at the response-handling step?", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2992", "reactions": [{"author": "dario", "emoji": "🤔"}]}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-06-26T12:08:32+00:00", "text": "Think that answers itself actually - streaming always forces online, so auto batch routing just doesn't come into it.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1858"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-06-26T12:16:31+00:00", "text": "Pulled up the Jun 23 sync notes, nothing in there about streaming", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2993"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T12:32:32+00:00", "text": "Routing makes sense now, though I'm not entirely sure cache behavior is the same story, does a streamed response get cached the same way a normal online response would, or does it bypass that?", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1859"}
{"channel": "code-review", "author": "dermot", "created_at": "2025-06-26T12:35:48+00:00", "text": "@Dario, might be worth your eyes on PR 693 given the retry question, if the stream drops mid-response, I'm not entirely sure how that interacts with caching-and-resume", "id": "m-code-review-2025-06-26-2994"}
{"channel": "pipeline", "author": "emil", "created_at": "2025-06-26T12:41:00+00:00", "text": "Routing's settled - streaming forces online, auto batch doesn't apply to it. Cache behavior is the remaining open piece; I pulled up the Jun 23 sync notes and they don't touch streaming at all, so probably worth looping in Dario since he owns caching-and-resume.", "id": "m-pipeline-2025-06-26-1860"}
